als and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Alabama remains one of the most Republican-leaning states in presidential politics, with a partisan lean of fifteen points toward the GOP. The seat is open, with the incumbent president term-limited, so neither party benefits from incumbency. No general-election polls or expert ratings are available for this race, and no fundraising figures are on record for either side.\n\nThe forecast therefore rests on the state's basic partisanship. National coverage notes that the president's approval is positive in only about ten states, and Democratic hopefuls have campaigned in the South, but nothing suggests Alabama's alignment is in play. The Republican nominee is a strong favorite; the real uncertainty is the size of the margin rather than who wins.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0488, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0924, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0912, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0912, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0824, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0837, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0865, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0895, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0869, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.087, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0756, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0829, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0893, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0877, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.078, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0805, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.0891, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.0834, "margin": -15.0}, {"dat